    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6282" root="جمر" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْمَرُ</span></b>  occurs in a trad., where it is said, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَخَلْتُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَسْجِدَ وَالنَّاسُ أَجْمَرُ مَا كَانُوا</span>, meaning <i>I entered
the mosque when the people were in their most
collected state.</i> (TA.)

